From 977385fbd7c8bce893adfa9690f6f65c1ff1a79d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:59:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 245/248] feat(desktop): grey 'waiting' stripe (card glyph)
 while a chat's kanban cards are open [daveey]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A chat that handed its work to kanban cards showed no stripe at all while
they ran. It now shows a grey card glyph (parked like the cron loop glyph,
skipped by ⌘]/⌘[); a blocked card still paints it red, a live turn wins.
The badge tooltip reads 'Waiting on N cards'.
